expect: written
note: written
floor: 2
keeps: width | four
why: the code names four attributes and the claim calls them "an attribute", so a reader has to go and find which; the remedy is their names, or their kind with the count as in "any of the four size attributes"; no check reaches this, since a generic noun is ordinary English, so judgement decides it and the floor is 2 of 5
labelled: 2026-09-21
--- code
export function sizeOf(track: LedgerTrack): Size | undefined {
  for (const key of ['width', 'height', 'bandwidth', 'frameRate'] as const) {
    if (typeof track[key] !== 'number' || track[key] <= 0) {
      return undefined;
    }
  }
  return { width: track.width, height: track.height };
}
--- facts
A posting is rejected where an attribute is absent or not positive, so this returns undefined there.
